elect the correct options in the following reasoning.For all $x\\in R,$  we have that\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}\\cdot 7\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,+\\,{{field-2}}\\cdot 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,+\\,{{field-3}}\\cdot (-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=0.\n$$\n\nSince \n{{field-4}} \nthe scalar coefficients in the linear combination are zero, the given set of functions is linearly \n{{field-5}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the set of functions ${{f}_{1}(x),{f}_{2}(x),…,{f}_{n}(x)},$ which are defined on some interval $I,$ is *linearly dependent* if there exist real scalars ${k}_{1},{k}_{2},…,{k}_{n}$ not all zero such that the linear combination ${k}_{1}\\cdot {f}_{1}+{k}_{2}\\cdot {f}_{2}+…+{k}_{n}\\cdot {f}_{n}$ is identically zero, i.e, \n\n$$\n{k}_{1}\\cdot {f}_{1}(x)+{k}_{2}\\cdot {f}_{2}(x)+…+{k}_{n}\\cdot {f}_{n}(x)=0\n$$\n\nfor all $x\\in I.$ Otherwise, if ${k}_{1}={k}_{2}=⋯={k}_{n}=0$ is the only solution, the set is *linearly independent*.\n\nNow, for all $x\\in R,$ we have that \n\n$$\n0\\cdot 7\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,+\\,4\\cdot 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,+\\,4\\cdot (-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $\\text{not all}$ the scalar coefficients in the linear combination are zero, the given set of functions is linearly $\\text{dependent}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-334021/field-1" "q-334021/field-2" "q-334021/field-3" "q-334021/field-4" "q-334021/field-5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe4c8bb4-b7c0-5afc-86fd-40c20df9b953"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334021"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186149736 :answer-field/correct 17592186149738 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186149740 :answer-field/correct 17592186149741 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186149732 :answer-field/correct 17592186149733 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333508/field-4/9c8ec06ed37ba9d8d4151c63887fec9387ac3171d616ead3fa2