2c2d8836642aabb0a" :answer-field/choices ["q-334108/field-3/a8a725fec0b63a3b8d6f4591903bfe81596da23bd6deceff5c00414df35bbd3f" "q-334108/field-3/988842f9ae7a51d1679b23c13893e9f8d3070ea423527b72c2d8836642aabb0a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334108" :question/id #uuid "64f4cde4-f8ab-5629-93ea-f22c06ec9430" :question/math-academy-id "q-334108" :question/problem "$$\n{y}_{1}(x)={x}^{3}-2x,\\,{y}_{2}(x)=10x-5{x}^{3},\\,x\\in R\n$$\n\nConsider the functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ above. Given that ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of the same second-order linear differential equation, select the correct options in the reasoning below.$\\,$ The Wronskian is $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})=$ \n{{field-1}}, which is\n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the set ${{y}_{1}(x),{y}_{2}(x)}$ is linearly \n{{field-3}} \non $R.$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose the functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ are defined on some interval $I.$\nThe Wronskian $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})$ of these functions is defined as\n\n$$\nW({y}_{1},{y}_{2})=|\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′} & {y}_{2}^{′}\\end{aligned}|={y}_{1}{y}_{2}^{′}-{y}_{2}{y}_{1}^{′}.\n$$\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- If $W\\ne 0$ for at least one $x\\in I,$ then ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are linearly independent.\n\n- If $W=0$ and it’s known that ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions to the same second-order linear differential equation, then ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are linearly dependent.\n\nIn our case, the Wronskian is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({y}_{1},{y}_{2}) & =|\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}-2x & 10x-5{x}^{3} \\\\ ({x}^{3}-2x)^{′} & (10x-5{x}^{3})^{′}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}-2x & 10x-5{x}^{3} \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-2 & 10-15{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =({x}^{3}-2x)(10-15{x}^{2})-(10x-5{x}^{3})(3{x}^{2}-2) \\\\  & =x({x}^{2}-2)\\cdot 5(2-3{x}^{2})-5x(2-{x}^{2})(3{x}^{2}-2) \\\\  & =5x({x}^{2}-2)(2-3{x}^{2})-5x({x}^{2}-2)(2-3{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =-15{x}^{5}+40{x}^{3}-20x-(-15{x}^{5}+40{x}^{3}-20x) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is $\\text{zero for all }x\\in R.$\n\nTherefore, the set ${{y}_{1}(x),{y}_{2}(x)}$ is linearly $\\text{dependent}$ on $R.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-334108/field-1" "q-334108/field-2" "q-334108/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd428707-bb32-58b2-8a51-09e330af0bb1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334108"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334109/field-1/d750d29f6ba305ee5725c84ae4d106456df4d528737e0be0ceb70b9858b2befa" :answer/id #uuid "a8146607-bff8-52ca-af71-3d067a09bb77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334109/field-1/396dc0b7f52d60cd77d04d7c992c41d54a8830a391b86c510a0ef2293ccd0183" :answer/id #uuid "5e6fa93b-af08-52fc-aed9-cbbcb9d592b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334109/field-1/61dd582464f025653293ef4e0f5b4d4bb22c6f166cdde2aeded7b1ba7a8c38f9" :answer/id #uuid "eee0cc2a-f9d4-58f1-94b4-8e8f9c3ff257" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334109/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "e39b7239-232e-5444-b7d3-4e04a491e2b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334109/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f164cff-bd6b-5910-a6ef-ee25d386d151" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-334109/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-334109/field-1/d750d29f6ba305ee5725c84ae4d106456df4d528737e0be0ceb70b9858b2befa" "q-334109/field-1/396dc0b7f52d60cd77d04d7c992c41d54a8830a391b86c510a0ef2293ccd0183" "q-334109/field-1/61dd582464f025653293ef4e0f5b4d4bb22c6f166cdde2aeded7b1ba7a8c38f9" "q-334109/field-1/d971375f57c56d8